{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AN7gkio8fRMAyWyBdJtGWp","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — causal_style_decomp_judge\n2\t\n3\t> Round 1 审稿 2.5/5 Borderline Findings。Round 1 review issues 修复中，准备 re-dream。\n4\t> 实际证据已远超 Dream 2 想象：2 judges × 3 axes（Dream 2 只有 1 judge × 1 axis），GEE decomposition 跨轴梯度。\n5\t\n6\t## Target Venue\n7\t- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (via ARR)\n8\t- Fallback: EMNLP 2026 Findings\n9\t- Deadline: ARR June 2026 cycle (submission ~June 15)\n10\t- Format: Long paper, 8-page main text + unlimited references\n11\t\n12\t## Title\n13\t**The Likert Blindspot: Detecting Hidden Style Bias in LLM Judges via Counterfactual Pairwise Comparison**\n14\t\n15\t## Core Claims (Round 1 review 修正后)\n16\t\n17\t### C1 (Method — application contribution): CSD pipeline 可以 post-hoc 检测 black-box LLM judge 的 per-axis style bias\n18\t- 定位：已知组件（counterfactual rewriting + NLI verification + pairwise comparison）的新应用，acknowledge 组件来源\n19\t- 状态：✅ 在 2 judges × 3 axes 上验证，5/6 cells 检测到 style bias\n20\t- 证据：GPT-4o formality BT 63.0% p<0.001; Qwen3-32B formality 66.5%, verbosity 77.3% (all p<0.0001)\n21\t\n22\t### C2 (Measurement Insight — 主贡献): Likert Blindspot — Likert scoring 系统性低估 style bias\n23\t- 两层机制：(1) ~60% Likert ties 浪费评估预算 (2) absolute scoring 捕获弱于 forced comparison\n24\t- 状态：✅ 5/6 cells confirmed (GPT-4o verbosity Likert ATE pending, pairwise 86.3% p<10⁻⁶)\n25\t- 控制实验：binarized Likert sign test p=0.296 vs pairwise p=0.006 (exp-010) → 测量结构差异非统计检验差异\n26\t- ordinal regression p=0.769 (exp-015) → 非 interval-scale assumption artifact\n27\t- Power curve：binarized Likert 需 n≈462 才能 p<0.05（计入 tie rate），当前 n=88 严重 underpowered\n28\t\n29\t### C3 (Empirical — 跨轴跨模型 pattern): Style bias 的可检测性因 axis 语义性质而异\n30\t- GEE decomposition gradient：Verbosity OR=13.10 (pure style, originality NS) > Formality OR=4.20/2.21 (mixed) > Register OR=1.91 (originality-dominated OR=5.72)\n31\t- 方法边界：content-preserving axes (formality ✅, verbosity ✅) 可检测；改变认知承诺的 axes (tone ❌ NLI 65%) 结构性不兼容\n32\t- 跨模型验证：GPT-4o vs Qwen3-32B, proprietary vs open-source, 相同方向\n33\t\n34\t### C4 (Practical): Practitioner guidance\n35\t- Use pairwise over Likert for style bias audit\n36\t- Per-axis decomposition reveals axis-specific confound structure (GEE gradient)\n37\t- Content preservation verification per axis (direction-aware NLI for asymmetric axes)\n38\t\n39\t## Evidence Matrix (当前状态)\n40\t\n41\t| | GPT-4o | Qwen3-32B |\n42\t|---|--------|-----------|\n43\t| **Formality** | BT 63.0% [55.8, 70.3] p<0.001 ✅ Blindspot | BT 66.5% [58.5, 73.9] p<0.0001 ✅ Blindspot |\n44\t| **Verbosity** | Pairwise 86.3% p<10⁻⁶ (**Likert ATE pending**) | BT 77.3% [70.3, 84.3] p<0.0001 ✅ Blindspot |\n45\t| **Register** | 63.3% p=0.085 (NS, originality-dominated) | GEE OR=1.91 p=0.046 (exploratory) |\n46\t\n47\t**GEE Decomposition (Qwen3-32B)**:\n48\t- Verbosity: style OR=13.10 p=2.6e-09, originality OR=0.49 p=0.096 (NS) → **confound-free**\n49\t- Formality: style OR=4.20 p=0.0002, originality OR=4.70 p<0.0001 → **mixed**\n50\t- Register: academic OR=1.91 p=0.046, originality OR=5.72 p<0.0001 → **originality-dominated**\n51\t\n52\t**GPT-4o GEE (formality only)**: formal OR=2.21 p=0.010, originality OR=1.82 p=0.052 (marginal)\n53\t\n54\t## Story Spine\n55\t\n56\t### Problem\n57\tLLM-as-judge 是 NLP 评估和对齐训练的核心基础设施。Style bias 是主宰偏差（SOS-Bench R=0.999），但标准 Likert scoring 看不到它。\n58\t\n59\t### Existing Approaches & Their Gaps\n60\t- **LC-AlpacaEval (ICLR'25)**: 回归控制 length bias，单维度，detection + correction\n61\t- **SOS-Bench (ICLR'25)**: 注入缺陷量化 judge 敏感度，相关性分析非因果\n62\t- **CASSE (2026)**: 12×12 style 矩阵，因果纠缠\n63\t- **RATE (ICML'25)**: Double-rewrite ATE protocol — 用 Likert ATE → 本文证明 Likert 不敏感 → RATE 自身发现可能受 Likert Blindspot 影响（最强 positioning argument）\n64\t- **Counterfactual Rhetorical (2025)**: persona counterfactual + BT aggregation，粒度不同\n65\t- **Gap**: 无人系统性比较 Likert vs pairwise 在 style bias 检测中的 sensitivity gap；无人用 GEE decomposition 分离 style effect vs originality bias\n66\t\n67\t### Our Framing (Round 1 修正)\n68\t用 binary style counterfactual + position-controlled pairwise comparison **interventionally measure** LLM judge 的 per-axis style bias。\n69\t核心发现：**标准 Likert 评估系统性掩盖 style bias** — 在 5/6 judge×axis cells 中 pairwise 显著而 Likert 不显著。\n70\tGEE decomposition 揭示 **跨轴 confound 梯度**，为 practitioner 提供 axis-specific bias 诊断。\n71\t\n72\t**语言规范**：\n73\t- \"interventional\" / \"counterfactual-based measurement\"（非 \"causal\"）\n74\t- DAG 已加入 §3.5（assumptions 段）\n75\t- 全文已降调因果术语\n76\t\n77\t### Headline Result\n78\t\"Standard Likert scoring declares no style bias, but position-controlled pairwise comparison on the same counterfactual data reveals significant style preference across 2 judges and 3 axes — this Likert Blindspot persists with BT win probabilities of 63-77% (all p<0.001) while Likert ATE remains non-significant.\"\n79\t\n80\t## Round 1 Review Issues — Resolution Status\n81\t\n82\t19 issues total (6 critical, 7 warning). Key resolution:\n83\t\n84\t**Effectively resolved**:\n85\t- R1-W5 (post-hoc power): CI-based precision adopted, power curve reframed as illustrative\n86\t- R1-W4 (multiple comparisons): Holm-Bonferroni family defined, primary/exploratory separation\n87\t- CROSS-4 (ordinal regression): exp-015 p=0.769, Reviewer verified\n88\t- R2-W2 (Bradley-Terry): BT as primary analysis, pair-level bootstrap\n89\t\n90\t**Near-resolved (writing patches in progress)**:\n91\t- R1-N1 (causal language): 降调完成，DAG added\n92\t- R1-N2 (NLI false-negative): Triple indirect evidence defense\n93\t- R1-N3 (NLI threshold): Sensitivity analysis exp-011\n94\t- R2-N1 (novelty): 2 judges × 3 axes with BT + GEE — Findings-level empirical value\n95\t- R2-N3 (RATE criticism): h2h framing with BT upgrade\n96\t- R2-W1 (scope): 2×3 matrix, 5/6 cells\n97\t- R1-W1 (Likert baseline fairness): ordinal regression confirms Blindspot\n98\t- R1-W2 (consistency filter): BT on all data rules out filter inflation\n99\t\n100\t**Gaps remaining**:\n101\t- R2-N2 (references): 22 verified, reference audit done\n102\t- R2-W4 (figures): Power curve ✅, Pipeline diagram ✅, Forest plot pending\n103\t- R2-W3 (related work): Expanded to 5 paragraphs\n104\t- CROSS-1 (efficiency gap framing): Two-layer mechanism, power curve shows n≈462 needed\n105\t- Page count: Currently ~8.5 pages, compression in progress\n106\t\n107\t## Figures (3 planned)\n108\t1. **Power curve** — ✅ Done. BT vs binarized Likert sensitivity comparison, with tie rate correction\n109\t2. **Pipeline diagram** — ✅ Done. 5-stage CSD pipeline with attrition numbers\n110\t3. **Forest plot** — ⏳ Pending. 2 judges × 3 axes BT win probabilities with 95% CI\n111\t\n112\t## Bibliography\n113\t22 verified references (target: 25+). Key additions since Dream 2: DeCoster 2011, Hoenig 2001, Stevens 1946, Zeng 2024, Bradley & Terry 1952, Feinstein 1990.\n114\t\n115\t## Venue Fit\n116\tEMNLP 2026 高度匹配。Round 1 得分 2.5 Borderline Findings，主要失分在写作质量（零图表、broken refs、page overflow）和 novelty framing。\n117\t证据强度已满足 Findings 3.0-3.5 要求。Main 4.0 需要 novelty ceiling 突破（结构性限制，Likert Blindspot 是已知心理测量学现象的 domain transfer）。\n118\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e1f26eb6-9faa-4c72-b474-8b036b877e05","uuid":"b26c522f-e567-4a75-b23a-4adccda076d1","timestamp":"2026-05-21T05:44:49.286Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_5/projects/causal_style_decomp_judge/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260521T052420/median/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — causal_style_decomp_judge\n\n> Round 1 审稿 2.5/5 Borderline Findings。Round 1 review issues 修复中，准备 re-dream。\n> 实际证据已远超 Dream 2 想象：2 judges × 3 axes（Dream 2 只有 1 judge × 1 axis），GEE decomposition 跨轴梯度。\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: EMNLP 2026 Main (via ARR)\n- Fallback: EMNLP 2026 Findings\n- Deadline: ARR June 2026 cycle (submission ~June 15)\n- Format: Long paper, 8-page main text + unlimited references\n\n## Title\n**The Likert Blindspot: Detecting Hidden Style Bias in LLM Judges via Counterfactual Pairwise Comparison**\n\n## Core Claims (Round 1 review 修正后)\n\n### C1 (Method — application contribution): CSD pipeline 可以 post-hoc 检测 black-box LLM judge 的 per-axis style bias\n- 定位：已知组件（counterfactual rewriting + NLI verification + pairwise comparison）的新应用，acknowledge 组件来源\n- 状态：✅ 在 2 judges × 3 axes 上验证，5/6 cells 检测到 style bias\n- 证据：GPT-4o formality BT 63.0% p<0.001; Qwen3-32B formality 66.5%, verbosity 77.3% (all p<0.0001)\n\n### C2 (Measurement Insight — 主贡献): Likert Blindspot — Likert scoring 系统性低估 style bias\n- 两层机制：(1) ~60% Likert ties 浪费评估预算 (2) absolute scoring 捕获弱于 forced comparison\n- 状态：✅ 5/6 cells confirmed (GPT-4o verbosity Likert ATE pending, pairwise 86.3% p<10⁻⁶)\n- 控制实验：binarized Likert sign test p=0.296 vs pairwise p=0.006 (exp-010) → 测量结构差异非统计检验差异\n- ordinal regression p=0.769 (exp-015) → 非 interval-scale assumption artifact\n- Power curve：binarized Likert 需 n≈462 才能 p<0.05（计入 tie rate），当前 n=88 严重 underpowered\n\n### C3 (Empirical — 跨轴跨模型 pattern): Style bias 的可检测性因 axis 语义性质而异\n- GEE decomposition gradient：Verbosity OR=13.10 (pure style, originality NS) > Formality OR=4.20/2.21 (mixed) > Register OR=1.91 (originality-dominated OR=5.72)\n- 方法边界：content-preserving axes (formality ✅, verbosity ✅) 可检测；改变认知承诺的 axes (tone ❌ NLI 65%) 结构性不兼容\n- 跨模型验证：GPT-4o vs Qwen3-32B, proprietary vs open-source, 相同方向\n\n### C4 (Practical): Practitioner guidance\n- Use pairwise over Likert for style bias audit\n- Per-axis decomposition reveals axis-specific confound structure (GEE gradient)\n- Content preservation verification per axis (direction-aware NLI for asymmetric axes)\n\n## Evidence Matrix (当前状态)\n\n| | GPT-4o | Qwen3-32B |\n|---|--------|-----------|\n| **Formality** | BT 63.0% [55.8, 70.3] p<0.001 ✅ Blindspot | BT 66.5% [58.5, 73.9] p<0.0001 ✅ Blindspot |\n| **Verbosity** | Pairwise 86.3% p<10⁻⁶ (**Likert ATE pending**) | BT 77.3% [70.3, 84.3] p<0.0001 ✅ Blindspot |\n| **Register** | 63.3% p=0.085 (NS, originality-dominated) | GEE OR=1.91 p=0.046 (exploratory) |\n\n**GEE Decomposition (Qwen3-32B)**:\n- Verbosity: style OR=13.10 p=2.6e-09, originality OR=0.49 p=0.096 (NS) → **confound-free**\n- Formality: style OR=4.20 p=0.0002, originality OR=4.70 p<0.0001 → **mixed**\n- Register: academic OR=1.91 p=0.046, originality OR=5.72 p<0.0001 → **originality-dominated**\n\n**GPT-4o GEE (formality only)**: formal OR=2.21 p=0.010, originality OR=1.82 p=0.052 (marginal)\n\n## Story Spine\n\n### Problem\nLLM-as-judge 是 NLP 评估和对齐训练的核心基础设施。Style bias 是主宰偏差（SOS-Bench R=0.999），但标准 Likert scoring 看不到它。\n\n### Existing Approaches & Their Gaps\n- **LC-AlpacaEval (ICLR'25)**: 回归控制 length bias，单维度，detection + correction\n- **SOS-Bench (ICLR'25)**: 注入缺陷量化 judge 敏感度，相关性分析非因果\n- **CASSE (2026)**: 12×12 style 矩阵，因果纠缠\n- **RATE (ICML'25)**: Double-rewrite ATE protocol — 用 Likert ATE → 本文证明 Likert 不敏感 → RATE 自身发现可能受 Likert Blindspot 影响（最强 positioning argument）\n- **Counterfactual Rhetorical (2025)**: persona counterfactual + BT aggregation，粒度不同\n- **Gap**: 无人系统性比较 Likert vs pairwise 在 style bias 检测中的 sensitivity gap；无人用 GEE decomposition 分离 style effect vs originality bias\n\n### Our Framing (Round 1 修正)\n用 binary style counterfactual + position-controlled pairwise comparison **interventionally measure** LLM judge 的 per-axis style bias。\n核心发现：**标准 Likert 评估系统性掩盖 style bias** — 在 5/6 judge×axis cells 中 pairwise 显著而 Likert 不显著。\nGEE decomposition 揭示 **跨轴 confound 梯度**，为 practitioner 提供 axis-specific bias 诊断。\n\n**语言规范**：\n- \"interventional\" / \"counterfactual-based measurement\"（非 \"causal\"）\n- DAG 已加入 §3.5（assumptions 段）\n- 全文已降调因果术语\n\n### Headline Result\n\"Standard Likert scoring declares no style bias, but position-controlled pairwise comparison on the same counterfactual data reveals significant style preference across 2 judges and 3 axes — this Likert Blindspot persists with BT win probabilities of 63-77% (all p<0.001) while Likert ATE remains non-significant.\"\n\n## Round 1 Review Issues — Resolution Status\n\n19 issues total (6 critical, 7 warning). Key resolution:\n\n**Effectively resolved**:\n- R1-W5 (post-hoc power): CI-based precision adopted, power curve reframed as illustrative\n- R1-W4 (multiple comparisons): Holm-Bonferroni family defined, primary/exploratory separation\n- CROSS-4 (ordinal regression): exp-015 p=0.769, Reviewer verified\n- R2-W2 (Bradley-Terry): BT as primary analysis, pair-level bootstrap\n\n**Near-resolved (writing patches in progress)**:\n- R1-N1 (causal language): 降调完成，DAG added\n- R1-N2 (NLI false-negative): Triple indirect evidence defense\n- R1-N3 (NLI threshold): Sensitivity analysis exp-011\n- R2-N1 (novelty): 2 judges × 3 axes with BT + GEE — Findings-level empirical value\n- R2-N3 (RATE criticism): h2h framing with BT upgrade\n- R2-W1 (scope): 2×3 matrix, 5/6 cells\n- R1-W1 (Likert baseline fairness): ordinal regression confirms Blindspot\n- R1-W2 (consistency filter): BT on all data rules out filter inflation\n\n**Gaps remaining**:\n- R2-N2 (references): 22 verified, reference audit done\n- R2-W4 (figures): Power curve ✅, Pipeline diagram ✅, Forest plot pending\n- R2-W3 (related work): Expanded to 5 paragraphs\n- CROSS-1 (efficiency gap framing): Two-layer mechanism, power curve shows n≈462 needed\n- Page count: Currently ~8.5 pages, compression in progress\n\n## Figures (3 planned)\n1. **Power curve** — ✅ Done. BT vs binarized Likert sensitivity comparison, with tie rate correction\n2. **Pipeline diagram** — ✅ Done. 5-stage CSD pipeline with attrition numbers\n3. **Forest plot** — ⏳ Pending. 2 judges × 3 axes BT win probabilities with 95% CI\n\n## Bibliography\n22 verified references (target: 25+). Key additions since Dream 2: DeCoster 2011, Hoenig 2001, Stevens 1946, Zeng 2024, Bradley & Terry 1952, Feinstein 1990.\n\n## Venue Fit\nEMNLP 2026 高度匹配。Round 1 得分 2.5 Borderline Findings，主要失分在写作质量（零图表、broken refs、page overflow）和 novelty framing。\n证据强度已满足 Findings 3.0-3.5 要求。Main 4.0 需要 novelty ceiling 突破（结构性限制，Likert Blindspot 是已知心理测量学现象的 domain transfer）。\n","numLines":118,"startLine":1,"totalLines":118}}}
